  "notes": [
    "Each row is the original when ...chat/click handler for that placement vnum; the text is the pinned English localization, not authored copy. Rows are keyed by vnum, so the model folder named in the original client npclist.txt and the server quest corpus agree by construction.",
    "The 20086/20087 model folders in the original client npclist.txt are reversed relative to the display names in mob_names_en.txt (model wondaim on Handu-Up, model handaup on Wonda-Rim). Spawn ids follow the model folder so they match the converted asset names.",
    "spawn.yongan.nnflower-20358-0 uses subquest_25.quest:160 instead of the oxevent.quest handlers, because every oxevent handler for 20358 is gated by pc.get_gm_level()==5 and is an event tool rather than player dialogue.",
    "Several rows are quest-conditional in the original (for example the Alchemist already-received branch, subquest_25 flower_done==0, warehouse.quest version 1 Storekeeper). The server has no quest-state gating yet, so the quoted branch is shown unconditionally until the matching quest chain lands.",
    "Titles are the say_title in force when the referenced line runs, which keeps the class-specific teacher titles instead of the wrong-class branch title.",
    "Six NPCs (Aranyo 20002, Ah-Yu 20003, Yonah 20005, Mirine 20006, Uriel 20011, Baek-Go 20018) are original wandering townsfolk: the client authorises no static point for them, so the server samples a point inside the pinned area and keeps it as an npc_spawn row. They carry dialogue rows exactly like static placements; the server resolves their board text from the area definition and their position from the sampled row.",
    "spawn.yongan.girl-lost-elder-brother-20006-0 and spawn.yongan.plant-researcher-20011-0 quote npc_talk.quest and main_quest_lv32.quest handlers whose original conditions branch on quest state (level 23..26 and the letter chain). The unconditional first line is quoted until that quest state exists."
  ],
